ickly.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike Dunleavy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Alaska's governorship is open for the first time in Dunleavy's two terms, with the Republican term-limited. Democrat Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins faces three Republicans: Treg Taylor, Bernadette Wilson, and Dave Bronson. Recent surveys across sponsors show Kreiss-Tomkins leading, with nonpartisan polls putting him at 52 to 55 percent and Republican-aligned polls showing narrower 3-to-8-point edges. Prediction markets price his chances in the low 80s, and rating outlets split between Tossup and Lean Democratic, with one calling it Likely Democratic.\n\nThe central dynamic is the divided Republican field. Trump endorsed Wilson and urged Taylor and Bronson to withdraw, but both stayed in through mid-October. Kreiss-Tomkins has also raised roughly two and a half times what Taylor has. Alaska's Republican lean and the possibility that ranked-choice voting consolidates Republican support keep this from being a stronger Democratic position.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6825, "margin": 2.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7395, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7331, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7068, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7071, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7313, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7365, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7094, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7204, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7496, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7614, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7414, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7753, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7728, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.